notes.body:
That's not true. For example the following code will lead to the use of an invalid address:
```
void *
wmem_array_index(wmem_array_t *array, guint array_index)
{
    ws_assert(array_index < array->elem_count);
    return &array->buf[array_index * array->elem_size];
}
```
Same goes with the check for the allocator scope that is now disabled, etc. We do not only have NULL pointer checks.

